cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "The proof is OpenAI's. If you use it, please cite OpenAI's paper and this archive."
title: "Finite-time blowup for Navier–Stokes: OpenAI's Lean proof, built and checked"
type: software
authors:
  - name: OpenAI
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-10
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/creelie/Erodos-breakthroug"
keywords:
  - Navier–Stokes equations
  - finite-time blowup
  - Millennium Prize Problem
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
abstract: >-
  OpenAI's Lean 4 proof of finite-time blowup for the forced three-dimensional
  Navier–Stokes equations (openai/NavierStokesAndEuler at f9e8bc5), unchanged, with
  a record of an independent build: both main theorems, alternatives (C) and (D) of
  the Clay problem description, depend only on propext, Classical.choice and
  Quot.sound, and their statements are identical to Google DeepMind's Formal
  Conjectures. The build record was made by Deep Bhattacharjee.
